 "type": "sampler",
 "summary": "M1-style two-oscillator sample synth: each oscillator plays waves from the song's wavetable (up to four key zones), into a 2-pole low-pass, ADSRs and two LFOs. For pianos, strings, brass and other multisampled sounds.",
 "quirks": [
  "Needs a wave: it plays the song's wavetable (OSC1 Wave defaults to slot 1) and is silent until that slot holds one (wave_import).",
  "A wave edited or replaced after it first played is cached: reload the machine to hear the change (README).",
  "MIDI notes (notes_write's default) take any of its 8 voices, a free one first, else the one released longest ago; a note's velocity does what the Volume column does (127 = full), through Amp Vel and Filter Vel (at 0 they ignore it); pitch bend moves every voice ±2 semitones, the mod wheel brings in LFO 1's vibrato (as LFO1 to Pitch, up to its maximum) and the sustain pedal holds released notes.",
  "Its Note track (notes_write with input \"tracks\") still plays as before, for old songs: a voice per track, its velocity the track Volume column; the 2026-11-03 profile heard a chord written there as one voice (U1: the multi-track note workaround, tier 3).",
  "It runs about 6 dB below other synths (README: internal headroom); raise Volume."
 ],
